<title>USA: U.S. Bancorp to focus on noninterest revs.</title>
<headline>U.S. Bancorp to focus on noninterest revs.</headline>
<dateline>PORTLAND, Ore. 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Bancorp said that in 1997, it will pay particular attention to noninterest revenue growth and active capital management.</p>
<p>U.S. Bancorp reported fourth quarter earnings of $0.79 a share, compared to $0.71 a share the previous fourth quarter, excluding special items in 1995.  </p>
<p>Noninterest revenue was $132.6 million in the fourth quarter, compared to $124.0 million the year before.</p>
<p>Net interest income was $394.1 million versus $363.1 million.</p>
